    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0888" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg788"/>

                <head>No. 501.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Señor Navarro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 11,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 28th ultimo, representing that certain bandits, headed by
                    one Robert Martin, have a haunt in the Sierra de la Hacha, in American
                    territory, on the Texas frontier, whence they make raids into Mexico for the
                    purpose of stealing cattle and bringing them on this side of the line.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have to express my regret that Mexican citizens in that quarter
                    should suffer from such depredations, and to state whatever measures may be in
                    the power of this government towards preventing them shall at once be taken.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
